    "note": "Sourced from \"Sr. Botany — My Baby Bullet-Q\" (Sri Publishers, STAR-Q Pass Track), book p.33, printed question 41. Botany-II holds only ONE source book: the TSBIE Basic Learning Material in hand covers physics only, and no Telangana Botany-II board paper is in the corpus, so the two-book union check and the board back-test are BOTH structurally impossible for this card — \"not checked\" does NOT mean \"checked and clean\". Run both the moment a second source or a real paper arrives. The mark split is a claim until a Telangana IPE teacher confirms it. BOOK ERROR, corrected on this card: the guide's p.33 figure labels BOTH panels \"In absence of inducer\". The second panel is the INDUCED state — its own content proves it, since lac mRNA is being transcribed, the three enzymes are being made and the repressor is drawn inactivated. The card labels it \"In the presence of inducer\". The guide also prints the gene map as \"p i p o z y a\"; the card uses the standard NCERT order i-p-o-z-y-a.\nThis is the second of only TWO questions in the paper whose marks sit on the drawing (the other is the chloroplast, global 17): the book prints no written answer here."
  },
  "insider_note": "Both panels or nothing. A single panel of the repressed operon answers half the question, because the whole point of an operon is that it switches.",
